MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_001: I suppose we may speak freely here. I believe\nsome discretion is in order.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_002: Now, then. You wanted to know why I have joined\nyour cause, correct?
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_003: It is only natural that a clergyman such as I... Heh.\nOh, were you expecting a fib?
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_004: You have already come to realize, I am sure, that this\nguise is nothing more than that. A guise.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_005: <NCA>"More or less."
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_006: <NCB>"Yes, but I want to hear your thoughts."
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_027: <ACA>
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_007: <ACA>Ah, yes. No matter the crisis, I do not think you\nwould accept those two in your ranks otherwise.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_008: <ACA>It is quite touching to see that my decision to let\nNuwa be has earned me your trust.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_009: <ACA>But I suspect what you wish to hear is my personal\nperspective and intentions.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_010: <ACB>I see. I am honored that you ask for my own thoughts\nand not the official Agarthan line.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_011: <ACB>You must certainly be wondering why I have\ncommitted myself to this course.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_012: Alright. Though you may think there is an ulterior\nmotive, I can assure you—there isn't.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_013: You want to know why I remain in Dagda and face\nhellfire to come to your aid?
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_014: Simply my own desire to do so. There is no agenda.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_015: Umm... Hm.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_016: Hahaha. I am not teasing you, I assure you.\nI am here of my own volition. Truly.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_017: A machine ordered me here. But then I encountered\nthe beasts of this land...that is to say, the humans.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_018: I expected to feel contempt but began instead to\ncultivate an appreciation for how freely they live.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_019: I realized I was living only for my mission and\nignoring the whispers of my own inner voice.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_020: Not the repressive voice of reason, but the\ninstinctive voice of desire.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_021: And as my thinking changed, along you came.\nI cannot say I know how you came to be.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_022: It pains me, abandoning my mission, but your goal of\nsaving a world beset by crisis is a noble one. 
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_023: Either way, I am delighted to see you fight the\nchildren of the goddess using their own power.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_024: This is to say that you yourself interest me. So I\nwill aid you.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_025: Not as a writhing fanatic, nor a selfless martyr. But\nas one who freely made his own choice. Superb, no?
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_A_026: I trust that you better understand me now. So I will\nstay the course, if you'll let me.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_001: Ah. I see you have returned to us. A pity.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_002: Yes, it is true that I came here in the very hope that\nI might meet you...
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_003: But even so, it is not an outcome I particularly like.\nThere is but one way to leave that place.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_004: The providence of a god—a miracle. Ah, well. So\nit is.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_005: For now, we may rejoice in our reunion. Having\nachieved our goal, we now reach an anticlimax.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_006: <NCA>"I'm glad to see you again."
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_007: <NCB>"But all that hard work!"
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_008: <ACA>Indeed. The grace of the goddess is humiliating to\nreceive, but I cannot deny it affords us this chance.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_009: <ACA>For my time with you to have ended—that is what\nwould leech away my joy.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_010: <ACB>Our opponent may well have swallowed the world\nwhole. It was indeed a struggle.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_011: <ACB>Yet somehow whenever I was by your side, I had\nno doubt we would prevail.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_012: <NCA>"Have you become honest with yourself?"
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_013: It is hard to say. I myself am unsure. But given that I\nam now acting according to my own will, perhaps so.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_014: All this having been said, what will you do now? It\nseems your mission is at an end from where I stand.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_015: Hm?
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_016: I see. Despite the fact that you saved the world, you\nhave no intention of stopping, do you?
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_017: It is to be a new quest. That is your nature, I\nsuppose...Promised One.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_018: Well, I see that you will do just as you like. That\nis an accusation I now level at myself as well.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_019: You're not very quick-witted, are you? I am offering\nto join you.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_020: <RSDS>If you continue to fight by your own will, I will\ncontinue to aid you by mine.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_021: In the end, what we are left with is the purity of\nour wills.
MID_SE_Ism_Fab_S_022: Shall we, Promised One? I look forward to the future,\nand to what you will achieve.